## Team workflows

**Feature branch, one developer.**  
Create or check out the feature branch yourself. Run Direct. When the plan is done, review the dirty tree, commit in the slices you want, then push with your normal remote workflow.

**Keep `main` clean while a plan runs.**  
Stay on `main` only long enough to start Safe from a clean HEAD. The run proceeds on `autopilot/<plan-slug>`. After you confirm the batch commit, review that branch. Merge it through the menu or a merge request you open yourself. Do not run Direct on `main`.

**Review each phase before the next one lands.**  
Use Cloud. Read `autopilot/<plan-slug>/phase-N` after each commit. If a phase is wrong, stop there. Later phases will not exist yet. Cherry-pick or merge the phase branches you accept.

**Handoff between people.**  
The plan holds the statuses and the recorded mode. The next person runs the same `/autopilot-plan` command with the same plan path. The agent should detect the partial progress and ask to continue. Tell them the mode if the plan note is missing. Do not start a second Safe or Cloud branch for the same plan unless the first run was abandoned.

**Failed phase.**  
Whoever picks up the work reads the report, fixes the blocker, and runs autopilot again on the same plan. Continue. Do not delete earlier Cloud phase branches unless the team agrees the commits are unwanted.
